      "worked_solution": "If a large data set is normally distributed, it should be approximately bell-shaped. \n\nAmong the given options, the only bell-shaped curve is the following:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14178098/assets/7b4069987a2f0aa2865f817c10a71bf2a2f1c1c39a43ba64cf1baf7a621a0a4d.png)\n\nIt's important to note that other bell-shaped distributions exist. Therefore, further tests on the data are required to confirm whether the underlying distribution is normal.",
