    "q-324311": {
      "dom_id": "step-q324311",
      "name": "Question 9",
      "problem": "The durations of direct flights on a certain route are normally distributed with a mean of $180$ minutes and a standard deviation of $20$ minutes. What is the probability that a randomly selected flight lasts more than $178$ minutes but less than $188$ minutes? **Round your answer to two decimal places**.\n\n*Hint: A table of values of $Φ(z)$ for different values of $z$ is given below, where $Φ(z)$ is the cumulative distribution function for the standard normal distribution. *\n\n<table align=\"center\">\n\n<tbody><tr>\n<th>\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"5\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr> \n  <th width=\"25%\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$z$</th>\n  <th bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,0.00\\,$</th>\n  <th bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,0.01\\,$</th>\n  <th bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,0.02\\,$</th>\n</tr>\n<tr> \n  <th bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,-0.2\\,$</th>\n  <td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.4207\\,$ </td>\n  <td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.4168\\,$ </td>\n  <td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.4129\\,$ </td>\n</tr>\n<tr> \n  <th bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,-0.1\\,$</th>\n    <td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.4602\\,$ </td>\n    <td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.4562\\,$ </td>\n    <td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.4522\\,$ </td>\n</tr>\n<tr> \n  <th bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,0.0\\,$</th>\n  <td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.5000\\,$ </td>\n  <td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.4960\\,$ </td>\n  <td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.4920\\,$ </td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n</th>\n\n<th width=\"5%\"></th>\n\n<th>\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"5\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr> \n  <th width=\"25%\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$z$</th>\n  <th bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,0.00\\,$</th>\n  <th bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,0.01\\,$</th>\n  <th bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,0.02\\,$</th>\n</tr>\n<tr> \n  <th bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,0.2\\,$</th>\n  <td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.5793\\,$ </td>\n  <td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.5832\\,$ </td>\n  <td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.5871\\,$ </td>\n</tr>\n<tr> \n  <th bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,0.3\\,$</th>\n    <td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.6179\\,$ </td>\n    <td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.6217\\,$ </td>\n    <td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.6255\\,$ </td>\n</tr>\n<tr> \n  <th bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,0.4\\,$</th>\n  <td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.6554\\,$ </td>\n  <td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.6591\\,$ </td>\n  <td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.6628\\,$ </td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n</th>\n\n</tr>\n\n</tbody></table>\n\nThe probability that a randomly selected flight lasts more than $178$ minutes but less than $188$ minutes is approximately\n{{field-1}}.",
      "worked_solution": "Let $X$ represent the flight duration (in minutes). Then we have $X∼N(180,{20}^{2}).$\n\nWe want to find $P(178<X<188).$ First, we convert $X$ to a standard normal random variable by $z$-scoring:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(178<X<188) & =P(\\frac{178-180}{20}<Z<\\frac{188-180}{20}) \\\\  & =P(-0.1<Z<0.4)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we express the required probability in terms of $Φ(z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(-0.1<Z<0.4) & =P(Z<0.4)-P(Z\\le -0.1) \\\\  & =P(Z\\le 0.4)-P(Z\\le -0.1) \\\\  & =Φ(0.4)-Φ(-0.1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the $z$-table, we see that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Φ(0.4) & =0.6554 \\\\ Φ(-0.1) & =0.4602.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(-0.1<Z<0.4) & =Φ(0.4)-Φ(-0.1) \\\\  & =0.6554-0.4602 \\\\  & =0.1952 \\\\  & ≈0.20\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the probability that a randomly selected flight lasts more than $178$ minutes but less than $188$ minutes is approximately $0.20.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
