    "q-324457": {
      "dom_id": "step-q324457",
      "name": "Question 13",
      "problem": "In a distribution center, the average weight of shipped packages is $2.5$ kilograms. However, $20%$ of packages weigh no more than $2.3$ kilograms. Assuming that package weights are normally distributed, find the standard deviation, $\\sigma ,$ of the package weights, **rounded to two decimal places.**\n\n*Hint: A table of values of ${Φ}^{-1}(p)$ for different values of $p$ is given below, where $p=Φ(z)$ is the cumulative distribution function for the standard normal distribution. *\n\n| $p$ | $\\,0.01\\,$ | $\\,0.03\\,$ | $\\,0.05\\,$ | $\\,0.10\\,$ | $\\,0.15\\,$ | $\\,0.20\\,$ | $\\,0.25\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${Φ}^{-1}(p)$ | $\\,-2.3263\\,$ | $\\,-1.8808\\,$ | $\\,-1.6449\\,$ | $\\,-1.2816\\,$ | $\\,-1.0364\\,$ | $\\,-0.8416\\,$ | $\\,-0.6745\\,$ |\n\n$\\sigma ≈$\n{{field-1}}\n$kg$",
      "worked_solution": "Let $X$ represent the package weight (in kilograms). Then we have $X∼N(2.5,{\\sigma }^{2}),$ and we want to find the standard deviation $\\sigma .$ \n\nWe know that $P(X\\le 2.3)=0.20.$ Converting $X$ to a standard normal random variable by $z$-scoring, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\le 2.3) & =0.20 \\\\ P(Z\\le \\frac{2.3-2.5}{\\sigma }) & =0.20 \\\\ Φ(-\\frac{0.2}{\\sigma }) & =0.20 \\\\ -\\frac{0.2}{\\sigma } & ={Φ}^{-1}(0.20).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the table, \n\n$$\n{Φ}^{-1}(0.20)=-0.8416.\n$$\n\nFinally then, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{0.2}{\\sigma } & =-0.8416 \\\\ \\frac{0.2}{\\sigma } & =0.8416 \\\\ \\sigma  & =\\frac{0.2}{0.8416} \\\\  & ≈0.24\\,\\text{kg}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
