    "q-95073": {
      "dom_id": "step-q95073",
      "name": "Question 16",
      "problem": "A group of students took a test and got an average score of $81.$ Additionally, $5%$ of the students scored greater than $91.$ Assuming that the students' scores are normally distributed, find the percent of students with a score lower than $70,$ rounded to $1$ decimal place.\n\n*Hint: A table of values of ${Φ}^{-1}(p)$ for different values of $p$ is given below, where $p=Φ(z)$ is the cumulative distribution function for the standard normal distribution. *\n\n| $p$ | $\\,0.900\\,$ | $\\,0.950\\,$ | $\\,0.975\\,$ | $\\,0.990\\,$ | $\\,0.995\\,$ | $\\,0.999\\,$ | $\\,0.9995\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${Φ}^{-1}(p)$ | $\\,1.2816\\,$ | $\\,1.6449\\,$ | $\\,1.9600\\,$ | $\\,2.3263\\,$ | $\\,2.5758\\,$ | $\\,3.0902\\,$ | $\\,3.2905\\,$ |\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\n*In addition, you're given the following table of values for $p=Φ(z)$*.\n\n| $z$ | $\\,0.00\\,$ | $\\,0.01\\,$ | $\\,0.02\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,-1.9\\,$ | $\\,0.0287\\,$ | $\\,0.0281\\,$ | $\\,0.0274\\,$ |\n| $\\,-1.8\\,$ | $\\,0.0359\\,$ | $\\,0.0351\\,$ | $\\,0.0344\\,$ |\n| $\\,-1.7\\,$ | $\\,0.0446\\,$ | $\\,0.0436\\,$ | $\\,0.0427\\,$ |",
      "worked_solution": "Let $X$ represent the grade obtained by a student. Then we have $X∼N(81,{\\sigma }^{2}),$ and we want to find $P(X<70).$ But first, we need to find the standard deviation $\\sigma .$ \n\nWe know that $P(X>91)=0.05.$ First, we convert this to a cumulative probability:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\le 91) & =1-P(X>91) \\\\  & =1-0.05 \\\\  & =0.95\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we convert $X$ to a standard normal random variable by $z$-scoring. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\le 91) & =0.95 \\\\ P(Z\\le \\frac{91-81}{\\sigma }) & =0.95 \\\\ Φ(\\frac{10}{\\sigma }) & =0.95 \\\\ \\frac{10}{\\sigma } & ={Φ}^{-1}(0.95)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the table, \n\n$$\n{Φ}^{-1}(0.95)≈1.6449.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{10}{\\sigma } & =1.6449 \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sigma } & =0.16449 \\\\ \\sigma  & =\\frac{1}{0.16449} \\\\  & ≈6.0794.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can solve for $P(X<70)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X<70) & =P(X\\le 70) \\\\  & =P(Z\\le \\frac{70-81}{6.0794}) \\\\  & ≈P(Z\\le -1.81) \\\\  & =Φ(-1.81) \\\\  & =0.0351 \\\\  & ≈3.5%\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, approximately $3.5%$ of the students scored lower than $70.$",
